1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,905
Ever since the day
I found out you were married,

2
00:01:02,985 --> 00:01:04,665
I've never dared cross the line.

3
00:01:04,745 --> 00:01:06,225
I came here today

4
00:01:06,305 --> 00:01:07,865
so you could rest easy.

5
00:01:07,945 --> 00:01:10,105
I think of Runch as a friend.

6
00:01:10,185 --> 00:01:12,945
What I did was wrong.
I'll treat you better.

7
00:01:13,025 --> 00:01:14,945
-I just need a roof over my head.
-No…

8
00:01:15,025 --> 00:01:16,345
-What? Honey!
-Mom!

9
00:01:16,425 --> 00:01:17,385
-Ging!
-Mom!

10
00:01:17,465 --> 00:01:20,385
You think you can fool me
by pretending to be nice?

11
00:01:21,985 --> 00:01:25,945
I'll have to show Runch
her mom's true colors.

12
00:01:26,025 --> 00:01:28,145
This is a war between a wife
and her mother-in-law.

13
00:01:28,905 --> 00:01:29,945
Yeah.

14
00:01:33,545 --> 00:01:35,345
Ms. Runch! Hello.

15
00:01:35,425 --> 00:01:37,065
You arrived just in time.

16
00:01:37,145 --> 00:01:39,065
Ms. Neen is inside. You may go in now.

17
00:01:39,865 --> 00:01:42,265
She's not in a very good mood, though.
So please beware.

18
00:01:43,105 --> 00:01:44,945
Is something wrong?

19
00:01:45,025 --> 00:01:47,785
It's about work.
Something didn't go her way.

20
00:01:49,065 --> 00:01:50,385
Okay.

21
00:01:51,425 --> 00:01:54,305
I bought two cakes. One's for you,

22
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:56,705
and please plate the other one for Neen.

23
00:01:57,785 --> 00:01:59,945
As for her tea, I'll bring it myself.

24
00:02:00,025 --> 00:02:03,865
Got it. Thank you kindly for the dessert.

25
00:02:04,585 --> 00:02:05,625
My pleasure.

26
00:02:12,105 --> 00:02:13,425
Yes, Nat?

27
00:02:30,585 --> 00:02:32,105
Runch!

28
00:02:33,985 --> 00:02:37,665
Nat told me her boss
is in a bad mood today.

29
00:02:39,185 --> 00:02:41,545
I hope my flowers

30
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:43,345
can cheer you up.

31
00:02:43,425 --> 00:02:44,905
Aw.

32
00:02:45,865 --> 00:02:47,785
They sure help.

33
00:02:49,945 --> 00:02:51,185
Smell so good too.

34
00:02:52,145 --> 00:02:55,865
Not as good as you, though.
You smell really good.

35
00:02:58,905 --> 00:03:00,985
Does that mean

36
00:03:02,025 --> 00:03:03,545
you're feeling better now?

37
00:03:05,265 --> 00:03:06,705
Just seeing your face is enough.

38
00:03:07,545 --> 00:03:09,065
-Is this mine?
-Yeah.

39
00:03:10,505 --> 00:03:13,825
There's cake too.
I asked Nat to plate it for you.

40
00:03:15,345 --> 00:03:17,265
How suspicious.

41
00:03:17,345 --> 00:03:19,705
Why'd you buy me
so much stuff all of a sudden?

42
00:03:20,305 --> 00:03:22,545
Is it some kind of special day?
I can't remember.

43
00:03:24,665 --> 00:03:26,665
I just wanted to.

44
00:03:40,785 --> 00:03:41,985
Here you go.

45
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:44,865
Please go ahead and feed each other.

46
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:46,705
I'm fine eating alone.

47
00:03:46,785 --> 00:03:48,225
Don't worry.

48
00:03:48,305 --> 00:03:51,225
I'll hook you up with guys and girls
here and there in our office.

49
00:03:51,305 --> 00:03:52,945
Whoa! No, thank you.

50
00:03:53,025 --> 00:03:54,465
No one's my type, though.

51
00:03:55,065 --> 00:03:57,345
Yet you complain that you're single.
You're so picky.

52
00:03:58,345 --> 00:04:00,305
Well, Ms. Runch comes to see you often.

53
00:04:00,385 --> 00:04:02,065
Anyone who's single would get jealous.

54
00:04:05,305 --> 00:04:07,425
Nat, if you're done with work for the day,

55
00:04:07,505 --> 00:04:09,065
you may go home.

56
00:04:09,145 --> 00:04:11,145
Okay. See you tomorrow.

57
00:04:11,225 --> 00:04:12,105
Okay.

58
00:04:19,825 --> 00:04:20,705
Come here.

59
00:04:28,305 --> 00:04:29,145
So good.

60
00:04:42,905 --> 00:04:44,025
Did I get some on my face?

61
00:04:46,305 --> 00:04:47,625
What's wrong?

62
00:04:51,305 --> 00:04:52,425
You're so pretty.

63
00:04:57,745 --> 00:04:59,625
-Runch.
-Yes?

64
00:05:00,145 --> 00:05:01,905
Can I ask you something?

65
00:05:02,505 --> 00:05:04,625
When your mom asked to stay at our place,

66
00:05:05,145 --> 00:05:07,185
she wasn't scheming anything, right?

67
00:05:12,905 --> 00:05:14,185
I don't think so.

68
00:05:14,265 --> 00:05:15,425
Really?

69
00:05:16,385 --> 00:05:20,105
It's probably typical of an old woman
who's upset with her husband.

70
00:05:29,785 --> 00:05:31,265
Hello, Mom.

71
00:05:32,025 --> 00:05:34,825
Dinner? Sure.

72
00:05:34,905 --> 00:05:37,025
Yes, I'm free. I'll bring Runch too.

73
00:05:39,145 --> 00:05:41,305
Okay. See you later.

74
00:05:41,385 --> 00:05:43,145
Sure. See you.

75
00:05:43,665 --> 00:05:44,625
Bye.

76
00:05:46,665 --> 00:05:49,745
Let me call my mom and tell her

77
00:05:49,825 --> 00:05:51,345
we'll be home late tonight.

78
00:05:51,425 --> 00:05:52,345
Sure.

79
00:05:58,265 --> 00:06:00,225
They're all Runch's favorites.

80
00:06:00,305 --> 00:06:02,025
I bet she'll love them.

81
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,065
Runch.

82
00:06:22,705 --> 00:06:25,425
You're having dinner
at Neen's parents' place?

83
00:06:27,825 --> 00:06:30,465
Of course. Please go ahead.

84
00:06:31,185 --> 00:06:33,585
Please tell everyone I miss them.

85
00:06:51,345 --> 00:06:53,425
Eat up, Runch.

86
00:06:53,505 --> 00:06:54,865
Thank you, Neen.

87
00:06:55,465 --> 00:06:56,665
Here.

88
00:06:57,905 --> 00:06:59,425
You eat up too.

89
00:06:59,505 --> 00:07:01,145
Thank you.

90
00:07:02,305 --> 00:07:06,465
Hey. You got some on your face.
Let me get that for you.

91
00:07:09,145 --> 00:07:12,225
It's the sauce. Right there.

92
00:07:25,265 --> 00:07:26,145
There. Beautiful.

93
00:07:26,225 --> 00:07:28,465
Thank you, my gorgeous wife.

94
00:07:29,505 --> 00:07:31,785
My pleasure.

95
00:07:39,545 --> 00:07:42,425
Hold on. Is there something we don't know?

96
00:07:43,265 --> 00:07:46,705
Yeah. Are you two really being lovebirds,

97
00:07:46,785 --> 00:07:48,625
or is this just an act?

98
00:07:53,345 --> 00:07:54,665
Runch,

99
00:07:55,585 --> 00:07:57,265
would you tell everyone?

100
00:08:00,745 --> 00:08:02,785
We've talked about it.

101
00:08:03,305 --> 00:08:05,425
We agreed to stay married.

102
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:09,145
-Yes, we did!
-Really?

103
00:08:09,945 --> 00:08:12,505
-Yes.
-We decided to stay together.

104
00:08:15,145 --> 00:08:17,585
I'm so happy to hear that.

105
00:08:17,665 --> 00:08:21,145
-That's fantastic. Right, honey?
-I'm happy too, honey.

106
00:08:21,225 --> 00:08:22,585
I really am.

107
00:08:23,265 --> 00:08:26,265
We'll finally be a real family.

108
00:08:28,425 --> 00:08:29,745
Way to go, my sister-in-law.

109
00:08:30,985 --> 00:08:32,904
-I'm very proud of you.
-Yeah.

110
00:08:33,425 --> 00:08:36,345
Dad, I think we should celebrate tonight.

111
00:08:36,425 --> 00:08:37,985
Sure!

112
00:08:38,784 --> 00:08:41,385
-You can't go home until you're drunk.
-Yeah!

113
00:08:41,465 --> 00:08:42,625
Nai, not again!

114
00:08:42,705 --> 00:08:43,825
It's only occasionally,

115
00:08:43,904 --> 00:08:45,545
-so it's fine.
-He's right.

116
00:08:46,065 --> 00:08:46,985
Don't be shy.

117
00:08:47,065 --> 00:08:49,985
-Go all out.
-Are you kidding me, Dad?

118
00:08:50,705 --> 00:08:51,545
Don't drink, honey.

119
00:08:53,865 --> 00:08:54,865
Ugh, Neen.

120
00:08:56,425 --> 00:08:58,065
I think you got some on your lips.

121
00:08:58,145 --> 00:09:00,145
Aw, honey.

122
00:09:00,225 --> 00:09:02,025
Come on.

123
00:09:05,345 --> 00:09:06,385
Let's celebrate, Dad.

124
00:09:06,465 --> 00:09:07,865
Cheers.

125
00:09:07,945 --> 00:09:09,185
Cheers.

126
00:09:14,425 --> 00:09:16,425
Why don't you join them?

127
00:09:18,465 --> 00:09:20,185
No, thanks.

128
00:09:20,265 --> 00:09:23,185
If I get drunk, who will drive us home?

129
00:09:24,065 --> 00:09:26,265
If you can't drive,
just stay the night here.

130
00:09:27,785 --> 00:09:29,385
Runch will probably refuse.

131
00:09:29,465 --> 00:09:30,465
Why?

132
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:32,985
Her mother's been staying with us.

133
00:09:33,585 --> 00:09:34,705
What?

134
00:09:36,465 --> 00:09:38,425
Sounds like a disaster.

135
00:09:38,505 --> 00:09:39,825
Not yet.

136
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:41,785
It's so quiet, actually.

137
00:09:41,865 --> 00:09:43,185
So unusually quiet.

138
00:09:43,905 --> 00:09:46,585
She's been behaving really well.

139
00:09:47,705 --> 00:09:48,785
But…?

140
00:09:54,665 --> 00:09:58,105
But I know it's fake.
I know she's pretending.

141
00:10:02,225 --> 00:10:03,745
So what are you going to do?

142
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:09,585
What I can do for now…

143
00:10:11,065 --> 00:10:14,185
is to do whatever it takes

144
00:10:14,265 --> 00:10:16,865
for her mom to show her true colors.

145
00:10:16,945 --> 00:10:19,145
Just don't be too harsh.

146
00:10:19,225 --> 00:10:20,745
I feel bad for Runch.

147
00:10:21,585 --> 00:10:25,585
She's still her mother, after all.
There's no cutting her off…

148
00:10:27,225 --> 00:10:29,785
no matter what her mother's like.

149
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:33,585
I know. That's the hardest part.

150
00:10:39,345 --> 00:10:41,585
Come on. Walk.

151
00:10:41,665 --> 00:10:43,105
-Hey, wait.
-Mom.

152
00:10:43,185 --> 00:10:44,425
What happened, Runch?

153
00:10:44,505 --> 00:10:46,345
-Mom.
-You're so drunk!

154
00:10:48,145 --> 00:10:50,265
She's probably happy,

155
00:10:50,345 --> 00:10:51,785
so she had quite a few.

156
00:10:51,865 --> 00:10:54,065
This is what you call "a few"?

157
00:10:55,105 --> 00:10:56,105
Runch.

158
00:10:56,185 --> 00:10:57,665
-Mom!
-Yeah?

159
00:10:58,305 --> 00:10:59,945
Why are you still up?

160
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:02,705
I was waiting for you to come home.

161
00:11:04,865 --> 00:11:06,785
Why would you wait?

162
00:11:07,305 --> 00:11:10,225
I'm all grown up now. I'm not a child.

163
00:11:11,065 --> 00:11:13,625
You'll always be a child to me.

164
00:11:13,705 --> 00:11:16,665
No matter what you do,
I'll always worry about you.

165
00:11:17,545 --> 00:11:18,785
But…

166
00:11:20,345 --> 00:11:21,785
-Runch?
-Hey.

167
00:11:21,865 --> 00:11:23,065
Runch!

168
00:11:23,785 --> 00:11:24,625
No!

169
00:11:28,865 --> 00:11:29,985
Runch.

170
00:11:39,465 --> 00:11:41,225
Good night, Mom.

171
00:11:41,305 --> 00:11:42,145
Come on.

172
00:11:44,865 --> 00:11:46,225
Good night.

173
00:12:24,625 --> 00:12:25,465
Here.

174
00:12:25,985 --> 00:12:27,985
Some hot ginger tea for Runch.

175
00:12:28,065 --> 00:12:29,625
It'll help with her nausea.

176
00:12:32,545 --> 00:12:36,345
Thank you, Mom.
But she's so drunk she fell asleep.

177
00:12:36,905 --> 00:12:38,905
Is this the way your family does things?

178
00:12:40,225 --> 00:12:41,705
What do you mean?

179
00:12:41,785 --> 00:12:45,185
You only brought her home
after she got that drunk.

180
00:12:48,265 --> 00:12:50,705
She's all grown up now, Mom.

181
00:12:50,785 --> 00:12:53,865
Plus, she had a really good time today.

182
00:12:53,945 --> 00:12:56,345
I don't want to stop her all the time.

183
00:12:57,105 --> 00:13:00,905
But as a wife, taking her home
isn't the only way to take care of her.

184
00:13:03,905 --> 00:13:06,825
I take care of her
whichever way she wants me to,

185
00:13:06,905 --> 00:13:09,505
not just the way someone else sees fit.

186
00:13:09,585 --> 00:13:11,505
I'm just worried about my daughter.

187
00:13:15,505 --> 00:13:19,185
Runch never used to drink this much
while she was with me.

188
00:13:21,345 --> 00:13:24,225
Maybe she didn't have the courage
to live life the way she wanted yet.

189
00:13:26,385 --> 00:13:29,305
I raised her myself. I should know best

190
00:13:29,385 --> 00:13:32,385
what's good for her and what's not.

191
00:13:33,425 --> 00:13:34,625
I believe you.

192
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:37,345
And I know how much you love her.

193
00:13:39,705 --> 00:13:43,345
But now, I am the one
who lives together with her

194
00:13:43,425 --> 00:13:44,745
every day.

195
00:14:24,825 --> 00:14:26,385
What's that noise, Runch?

196
00:14:49,185 --> 00:14:52,225
Mom! Mom!

197
00:14:53,265 --> 00:14:54,105
Mom!

198
00:15:04,065 --> 00:15:05,025
Mom.

199
00:15:06,225 --> 00:15:07,585
Mom!

200
00:15:07,665 --> 00:15:09,625
Oh! Up already, honey?

201
00:15:09,705 --> 00:15:12,105
Your vacuuming woke us up, Mom.

202
00:15:12,185 --> 00:15:14,585
Ah! Oh dear. I'm sorry.

203
00:15:14,665 --> 00:15:16,265
It's just that I woke up early

204
00:15:16,345 --> 00:15:18,985
and I didn't want to lie in bed.
I wanted to do something,

205
00:15:19,065 --> 00:15:21,585
so I figured I should
clean the house a bit.

206
00:15:21,665 --> 00:15:23,905
Actually, you didn't have to.

207
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:25,665
The maid will be here anyway.

208
00:15:25,745 --> 00:15:28,265
That won't do, Runch. I'm staying here,

209
00:15:28,345 --> 00:15:31,585
and I don't want to just sit around
doing nothing every day.

210
00:15:32,505 --> 00:15:35,745
I want to help.
I don't want to be a burden.

211
00:15:43,865 --> 00:15:45,065
Mom?

212
00:15:46,865 --> 00:15:48,025
What's this?

213
00:15:51,625 --> 00:15:55,145
That's a photo of me and Runch.
I brought it along.

214
00:15:55,225 --> 00:15:57,905
I just love this photo.

215
00:15:57,985 --> 00:15:59,665
That's why I wanted to put it here.

216
00:15:59,745 --> 00:16:02,185
Why didn't you put it in your room?

217
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,745
I think this is a good spot, though. Here.

218
00:16:06,385 --> 00:16:08,465
See? It's a common area.

219
00:16:08,545 --> 00:16:09,745
Your guests will see it too.

220
00:16:11,065 --> 00:16:14,425
You're right! Anyone who enters the house

221
00:16:14,505 --> 00:16:18,505
will see these and be able to tell
who Runch is happier with.

222
00:16:20,425 --> 00:16:21,745
You're right!

223
00:16:23,945 --> 00:16:25,745
You're right, Neen.

224
00:16:49,385 --> 00:16:51,505
What's with the outfits?

225
00:16:51,585 --> 00:16:55,025
We're treating ourselves
to your favorite restaurant.

226
00:16:55,105 --> 00:16:56,545
I'll book us a table.

227
00:16:59,985 --> 00:17:02,265
I don't think we can today.

228
00:17:03,585 --> 00:17:04,785
Why not?

229
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:08,305
Well, my mom's cooking.

230
00:17:10,545 --> 00:17:13,345
Let's eat in today.

231
00:17:14,184 --> 00:17:16,385
We can eat out another day.

232
00:17:16,464 --> 00:17:17,345
Okay?

233
00:17:18,224 --> 00:17:19,625
Please?

234
00:17:25,985 --> 00:17:27,025
Sure.

235
00:17:28,305 --> 00:17:31,465
Then I'm helping her out.

236
00:17:44,345 --> 00:17:46,545
Can I help you with anything?

237
00:18:02,345 --> 00:18:04,665
Should I chop something up?

238
00:18:05,665 --> 00:18:07,865
Can you chop the chicken
on the cutting board?

239
00:18:13,145 --> 00:18:15,265
So sorry, Mom.

240
00:18:27,345 --> 00:18:30,105
Alright. Now that we're alone together,

241
00:18:30,825 --> 00:18:34,225
why don't you just tell me what you want?

242
00:18:34,305 --> 00:18:37,465
I should ask you the same thing.

243
00:18:40,185 --> 00:18:42,225
You picked a fight with your husband

244
00:18:42,305 --> 00:18:45,545
and faked being sad
in order to move in with us, right?

245
00:18:51,545 --> 00:18:54,225
No answer. That means I was right.

246
00:19:00,225 --> 00:19:02,425
You're so smart.

247
00:19:08,065 --> 00:19:09,985
I'll be honest with you.

248
00:19:10,065 --> 00:19:14,305
I'll do whatever it takes
to get you out of Runch's life.

249
00:19:15,665 --> 00:19:20,265
Do whatever you want.
Runch will choose me anyway, Mom.

250
00:19:21,505 --> 00:19:22,505
Sure.

251
00:19:23,305 --> 00:19:25,865
Then let's have a cooking competition.

252
00:19:25,945 --> 00:19:28,465
Let's see who Runch will choose.

253
00:19:30,545 --> 00:19:32,305
Game on, Mom.

254
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:22,945
This kind of dish takes
good understanding to cook,

255
00:21:23,025 --> 00:21:24,425
not just a recipe.

256
00:21:25,185 --> 00:21:28,865
True. Being with her every day taught me
how to season certain dishes right.

257
00:21:38,425 --> 00:21:41,065
Smells amazing! What are you making?

258
00:21:41,585 --> 00:21:44,185
Neen and I are cooking together.

259
00:21:45,025 --> 00:21:47,185
Yeah. It's so much fun.

260
00:21:47,905 --> 00:21:48,985
Look.

261
00:21:49,065 --> 00:21:50,865
I made salted fish fried rice.

262
00:21:50,945 --> 00:21:52,985
Your childhood favorite dish.

263
00:21:53,065 --> 00:21:54,225
As for me,

264
00:21:54,305 --> 00:21:57,345
I made you truffle pasta.
You said it was your comfort food.

265
00:21:57,865 --> 00:21:59,705
Lucky me!

266
00:21:59,785 --> 00:22:01,585
I get to eat two very good dishes.

267
00:22:02,225 --> 00:22:03,345
-Yes!
-Yes!

268
00:22:06,505 --> 00:22:07,945
-Dig in.
-Dig in.

269
00:22:42,625 --> 00:22:44,305
What's wrong, Runch?

270
00:22:44,385 --> 00:22:45,825
It's so salty!

271
00:23:03,825 --> 00:23:05,305
It really is!

272
00:23:25,465 --> 00:23:27,145
What, Runch?

273
00:23:28,745 --> 00:23:30,425
This one's salty too.

274
00:23:30,505 --> 00:23:31,785
Is it?

275
00:23:47,705 --> 00:23:49,225
Why is it so salty?

276
00:23:53,785 --> 00:23:56,345
All in all, everything's delicious.

277
00:23:56,425 --> 00:24:00,585
It just takes a little imagination.

278
00:24:07,305 --> 00:24:08,425
Here you go, Neen,

279
00:24:08,505 --> 00:24:11,505
Runch. I packed you some lunch.

280
00:24:12,105 --> 00:24:14,865
It's to compensate for how
I didn't cook well yesterday.

281
00:24:14,945 --> 00:24:16,705
I don't want to bother you.

282
00:24:17,265 --> 00:24:18,665
It was no bother.

283
00:24:19,465 --> 00:24:21,185
I made it for you both.

284
00:24:21,265 --> 00:24:22,705
I put my heart into it.

285
00:24:22,785 --> 00:24:27,385
You two can share it. And let me know
if you ever want something in particular.

286
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:30,465
I'll gladly make you anything.

287
00:24:30,545 --> 00:24:31,585
Okay, Mom.

288
00:24:35,945 --> 00:24:36,785
Let's go.

289
00:24:37,305 --> 00:24:39,145
I'd better get to work.

290
00:24:39,825 --> 00:24:41,185
See you.

291
00:24:41,265 --> 00:24:42,985
Enjoy your lunch.

292
00:24:43,065 --> 00:24:44,185
Of course.

293
00:24:51,745 --> 00:24:52,945
Neen.

294
00:24:56,145 --> 00:24:58,305
You should give it to your coworkers.

295
00:25:00,545 --> 00:25:04,065
Why? My mom made it for you.

296
00:25:04,145 --> 00:25:06,505
Is it okay if I refuse her kindness?

297
00:25:06,585 --> 00:25:09,385
To be honest, I don't trust your mom.

298
00:25:09,465 --> 00:25:10,865
But Neen,

299
00:25:11,385 --> 00:25:14,465
my mom's trying to be a better person.

300
00:25:14,545 --> 00:25:16,545
It's clearly an act.

301
00:25:16,625 --> 00:25:17,865
Neen.

302
00:25:18,385 --> 00:25:20,545
Don't. It's too early
for us to be fighting.

303
00:25:23,065 --> 00:25:24,865
I'm not picking a fight.

304
00:25:25,865 --> 00:25:29,145
I just wish you'd give her a chance.

305
00:25:30,825 --> 00:25:32,265
Can I not?

306
00:25:32,345 --> 00:25:35,305
Whatever. I'm off to work.
See you in the evening.

307
00:26:00,705 --> 00:26:02,225
Neen, you're home!

308
00:26:02,305 --> 00:26:03,985
What's all this?

309
00:26:04,505 --> 00:26:06,745
They're plants and trees.
Don't you know what they are?

310
00:26:06,825 --> 00:26:10,465
I know what they are,
but why'd you bring so many?

311
00:26:10,545 --> 00:26:13,385
Well, they're all lucky plants.

312
00:26:13,465 --> 00:26:17,505
The canna lily brings peace to the family.

313
00:26:17,585 --> 00:26:18,985
This one,

314
00:26:19,865 --> 00:26:22,945
the water jasmine, protects us from evil.

315
00:26:25,345 --> 00:26:28,425
The tamarind tree wards off evil spirits.

316
00:26:29,025 --> 00:26:30,905
This way, our house
will be free of bad luck.

317
00:26:31,585 --> 00:26:32,585
What do you think?

318
00:26:33,585 --> 00:26:36,025
You're the bad luck in this house.

319
00:26:36,105 --> 00:26:39,185
Oh my! Why would you say that to me?

320
00:26:39,265 --> 00:26:40,745
Isn't it true, though?

321
00:26:40,825 --> 00:26:43,945
Runch isn't here, Mom.
So you can drop the act.

322
00:26:44,745 --> 00:26:47,625
There's no way I'd believe
you can really change.

323
00:26:48,625 --> 00:26:49,825
Neen,

324
00:26:50,345 --> 00:26:53,345
let's be reasonable here.
Why get emotional?

325
00:26:53,865 --> 00:26:56,425
I really am trying to treat you better.

326
00:26:57,665 --> 00:27:00,345
Stop putting on an act already, Mom.
It's making me sick.

327
00:27:00,425 --> 00:27:02,905
Why do you have to be so mean?

328
00:27:03,945 --> 00:27:06,465
I know

329
00:27:06,545 --> 00:27:09,985
I've wronged you. That's why you hate me.

330
00:27:10,065 --> 00:27:13,505
But now, I really do feel bad about it.

331
00:27:14,985 --> 00:27:17,465
I don't believe you,
and there's no way I will.

332
00:27:17,545 --> 00:27:20,865
Get all those trees out of here.
I don't like them.

333
00:27:22,585 --> 00:27:24,945
Neen, Neen!

334
00:27:25,025 --> 00:27:27,945
Don't go yet! Please listen to me, honey.

335
00:27:28,025 --> 00:27:30,145
Please listen to me!

336
00:27:30,825 --> 00:27:32,225
Neen!

337
00:27:35,625 --> 00:27:37,705
NEW RECORDING 5

338
00:27:39,705 --> 00:27:42,705
I'm always one step ahead of you,
you naive girl.

339
00:27:52,585 --> 00:27:54,105
What?

340
00:27:54,185 --> 00:27:55,945
Why are you sitting outside?

341
00:27:56,465 --> 00:27:58,185
I'm too scared to go inside.

342
00:27:58,785 --> 00:28:00,905
Why? What happened?

343
00:28:06,305 --> 00:28:09,905
Oh, Runch! Why are you home so late?
I've been waiting to have dinner with you.

344
00:28:09,985 --> 00:28:11,225
I'm starving.

345
00:28:11,745 --> 00:28:14,025
Did you have a fight with Mom?

346
00:28:20,905 --> 00:28:22,665
Did that old hag say something?

347
00:28:24,505 --> 00:28:27,705
Neen. Don't call my mom that.

348
00:28:27,785 --> 00:28:29,105
That's not very nice.

349
00:28:30,145 --> 00:28:33,305
So what did she say I did? Tell me.

350
00:28:35,185 --> 00:28:38,185
Well, it's about the plants and trees.

351
00:28:39,345 --> 00:28:43,185
My mom means well.
She just wants to bring us good luck.

352
00:28:44,745 --> 00:28:48,065
-Please let her plant them.
-Did she really tell on me over that?

353
00:28:48,145 --> 00:28:51,145
She didn't. She was just
telling me about it.

354
00:28:51,665 --> 00:28:53,785
You know, she really cares
about what you think.

355
00:28:53,865 --> 00:28:54,985
Really?

356
00:28:55,065 --> 00:28:56,625
This shows that she cares?

357
00:28:56,705 --> 00:28:59,185
If she really cared,
she should've asked me

358
00:28:59,265 --> 00:29:01,385
before planting them at our place.

359
00:29:02,905 --> 00:29:06,465
Whatever. She can plant
whatever she wants. I don't care anymore.

360
00:29:07,185 --> 00:29:09,505
-Don't be mad, Neen.
-Of course I am.

361
00:29:09,585 --> 00:29:10,745
I'm so mad.

362
00:29:10,825 --> 00:29:14,385
Whenever things don't get her way,
she tells on me to you. I hate that.

363
00:29:14,985 --> 00:29:17,465
We're all grown-ups here. We aren't kids.

364
00:29:18,065 --> 00:29:19,785
Well, I'm sorry on her behalf.

365
00:29:20,665 --> 00:29:23,785
Your mom's the one who should apologize,
not you.

366
00:29:25,145 --> 00:29:26,545
I'm done with this conversation.

367
00:29:27,065 --> 00:29:28,745
Okay, okay.

368
00:29:28,825 --> 00:29:31,665
I'll stop. Let's have dinner, shall we?

369
00:29:32,785 --> 00:29:34,905
I'm not hungry anymore. I'm not eating.

370
00:29:56,985 --> 00:29:58,345
Hello.

371
00:29:58,425 --> 00:30:01,225
Oh, hello. Uh…

372
00:30:01,305 --> 00:30:02,865
I'm Runchlaphat's mother.

373
00:30:03,385 --> 00:30:06,145
You mean Ms. Runch, the beautiful lawyer?

374
00:30:06,225 --> 00:30:08,545
Yes, that's her.

375
00:30:08,625 --> 00:30:10,585
I've been staying at her place lately.

376
00:30:12,865 --> 00:30:14,665
Why don't we talk inside?

377
00:30:17,225 --> 00:30:18,985
That's for you to take home.

378
00:30:19,585 --> 00:30:21,425
Thank you.

379
00:30:21,505 --> 00:30:24,905
My daughter works hard.
Some days she comes home late.

380
00:30:24,985 --> 00:30:27,145
That's why I usually cook her something.

381
00:30:27,225 --> 00:30:30,065
It's better than eating out
at restaurants.

382
00:30:30,145 --> 00:30:31,625
Those foods are full of MSG.

383
00:30:34,585 --> 00:30:38,425
Doesn't Ms. Runch's wife cook for her?

384
00:30:39,825 --> 00:30:43,665
Don't get me started.
Neen doesn't really do any of that.

385
00:30:45,025 --> 00:30:46,145
But I can't blame her.

386
00:30:46,225 --> 00:30:49,145
I get that she's busy with work.
But even so,

387
00:30:49,225 --> 00:30:51,625
she'll go out to party with her friends
and get home late,

388
00:30:51,705 --> 00:30:54,145
and my daughter
would have to take care of her.

389
00:30:56,945 --> 00:30:58,425
Please try it.

390
00:30:58,505 --> 00:31:00,025
I'm not that good a cook,

391
00:31:00,105 --> 00:31:02,265
but I do try my best for my daughter.

392
00:31:02,785 --> 00:31:04,225
How sweet.

393
00:31:04,305 --> 00:31:07,145
Ms. Runch sure is lucky
to have a mother like you.

394
00:31:08,385 --> 00:31:11,625
It's all I can do as a mother.

395
00:31:19,185 --> 00:31:21,145
Wake up.

396
00:31:23,425 --> 00:31:24,705
What's up?

397
00:31:26,025 --> 00:31:26,865
Come on.

398
00:31:26,945 --> 00:31:29,185
Let's go work out.

399
00:31:30,345 --> 00:31:33,105
-Let's go.
-No. Let me sleep.

400
00:31:37,665 --> 00:31:40,185
Neen, are you still mad at me?

401
00:31:49,585 --> 00:31:50,985
That's enough.

402
00:31:52,105 --> 00:31:53,305
No, it's not.

403
00:31:53,865 --> 00:31:55,945
Not until you forgive me.

404
00:31:58,905 --> 00:32:02,625
Okay, okay! I give up!

405
00:32:03,665 --> 00:32:05,065
Do you forgive me yet?

406
00:32:07,425 --> 00:32:08,785
Fine, I forgive you.

407
00:32:09,305 --> 00:32:10,745
You really are something.

408
00:32:13,185 --> 00:32:14,225
Come on.

409
00:32:14,305 --> 00:32:17,185
Let's go exercise, shall we?

410
00:32:31,625 --> 00:32:33,705
Come on. Up.

411
00:32:34,465 --> 00:32:35,505
Yay!

412
00:32:35,585 --> 00:32:37,385
Let's go!

413
00:32:44,625 --> 00:32:45,705
Why are you smiling?

414
00:32:46,985 --> 00:32:48,785
Did you forget something?

415
00:32:49,305 --> 00:32:50,265
What?

416
00:32:59,345 --> 00:33:00,665
This.

417
00:33:01,225 --> 00:33:02,705
I almost forgot.

418
00:33:03,305 --> 00:33:06,585
How could you? It means so much to us.

419
00:33:07,905 --> 00:33:09,305
It's crazy to think

420
00:33:09,385 --> 00:33:12,985
that we'll be each other's wives
in just a few months.

421
00:33:13,065 --> 00:33:14,225
Yeah.

422
00:33:14,785 --> 00:33:17,225
We've almost been together for two years.

423
00:33:17,305 --> 00:33:19,465
Time flies, doesn't it?

424
00:33:19,545 --> 00:33:20,665
It sure does.

425
00:33:23,265 --> 00:33:24,105
Neen.

426
00:33:27,465 --> 00:33:28,865
What's that, Runch?

427
00:33:31,305 --> 00:33:32,505
What?

428
00:33:43,985 --> 00:33:45,385
They're watches.

429
00:33:46,385 --> 00:33:48,305
But they're not meant

430
00:33:48,385 --> 00:33:52,025
to tell how much time has passed.

431
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:56,825
Instead, they'll remind me
that with every step I take,

432
00:33:56,905 --> 00:33:58,665
you'll always be there with me.

433
00:33:59,825 --> 00:34:02,945
How sweet. Thank you, Runch.

434
00:34:04,385 --> 00:34:05,705
Can you help me put it on?

435
00:34:06,705 --> 00:34:09,185
Of course. Here.

436
00:34:16,865 --> 00:34:18,065
There.

437
00:34:18,145 --> 00:34:19,145
Ready?

438
00:34:19,784 --> 00:34:22,065
Now we can jog together.

439
00:34:22,665 --> 00:34:23,585
Let's go.

440
00:34:29,865 --> 00:34:31,065
Runch!

441
00:34:33,985 --> 00:34:36,145
-Are you good?
-Yeah.

442
00:34:36,985 --> 00:34:38,705
I'm getting thirsty.

443
00:34:40,585 --> 00:34:42,784
Can you get me some water?

444
00:34:42,865 --> 00:34:44,784
Of course.

445
00:34:45,304 --> 00:34:46,625
I'll be right back.

446
00:34:46,705 --> 00:34:47,625
Okay.

447
00:34:47,705 --> 00:34:51,425
See? Just like Ms. Runch's mother said.

448
00:34:52,425 --> 00:34:54,105
-What did she say?
-Oh,

449
00:34:54,185 --> 00:34:56,065
she said she doesn't
take care of her wife.

450
00:34:56,145 --> 00:34:59,465
See? She's thirsty, but instead
of getting her own water,

451
00:34:59,545 --> 00:35:00,825
she's making her wife do it.

452
00:35:01,945 --> 00:35:04,265
That's not how a good wife should be.

453
00:35:04,345 --> 00:35:05,705
Exactly.

454
00:35:05,785 --> 00:35:09,025
She just sits back
and lets her wife do everything.

455
00:35:09,105 --> 00:35:11,305
That's why Runch's mother cooks for her,

456
00:35:11,385 --> 00:35:13,585
otherwise she'd have nothing good to eat.

457
00:35:13,665 --> 00:35:15,105
-Really?
-Yeah.

458
00:35:22,425 --> 00:35:24,025
Oh, Neen.

459
00:35:24,105 --> 00:35:25,665
So thirsty you couldn't wait, huh?

460
00:35:25,745 --> 00:35:27,265
Did you badmouth me to my neighbors?

461
00:35:28,905 --> 00:35:31,185
What are you talking about?
I don't understand.

462
00:35:31,265 --> 00:35:33,105
Stop acting so innocent.

463
00:35:33,185 --> 00:35:35,585
What'd you say to make them think
I don't take care of Runch?

464
00:35:36,785 --> 00:35:39,625
I didn't. Don't lie about me like that.

465
00:35:39,705 --> 00:35:43,105
Lie about you? I heard
what they said with my own ears!

466
00:35:43,185 --> 00:35:44,145
Say you did it!

467
00:35:44,225 --> 00:35:46,025
-Come on, say it!
-Neen!

468
00:35:46,105 --> 00:35:48,105
Neen, let go. You're hurting me.

469
00:35:48,185 --> 00:35:50,945
Neen, please let go of her.
You're hurting her for real.

470
00:35:51,025 --> 00:35:54,065
I won't let go
until your mom tells the truth.

471
00:35:54,145 --> 00:35:56,065
Stop bullshitting me! Stop it!

472
00:35:56,145 --> 00:35:58,065
-Stop it!
-Neen, that's enough!

473
00:36:06,705 --> 00:36:08,225
Did you just yell at me?

474
00:36:10,145 --> 00:36:11,385
I'm sorry.

475
00:36:13,265 --> 00:36:16,825
I didn't mean to, but you wouldn't listen.

476
00:36:16,905 --> 00:36:19,825
You say I wouldn't listen,
but you wouldn't either.

477
00:36:24,065 --> 00:36:25,865
Or do you think I was lying?

478
00:36:29,425 --> 00:36:30,425
Okay.

479
00:36:31,985 --> 00:36:34,785
Then you can stay with her all you want.

480
00:36:37,065 --> 00:36:38,665
Neen, wait--

481
00:36:42,705 --> 00:36:43,745
Mom.

482
00:36:44,705 --> 00:36:48,185
Runch, just go after her.
Don't worry about me.

483
00:36:49,185 --> 00:36:51,345
How could I go when you're like this?

484
00:36:52,625 --> 00:36:54,265
I'll get you an inhaler.

485
00:36:55,145 --> 00:36:56,145
Okay, honey.

486
00:37:09,185 --> 00:37:11,505
You just told me you're staying married,

487
00:37:11,585 --> 00:37:14,265
and now you had such a bad fight
you ran away from home?

488
00:37:14,345 --> 00:37:16,825
Well, Runch was the one
who was being unreasonable.

489
00:37:18,345 --> 00:37:20,985
But from what you told me,
you went too far.

490
00:37:21,065 --> 00:37:23,865
You insulted her mother.
How could she not be upset?

491
00:37:23,945 --> 00:37:26,345
What? It was her fault, though.

492
00:37:26,425 --> 00:37:29,585
I don't like being accused
when I didn't do anything wrong.

493
00:37:29,665 --> 00:37:32,865
So what are you going to do?
Stay here and not go home?

494
00:37:32,945 --> 00:37:34,065
Yes.

495
00:37:35,665 --> 00:37:39,145
I won't go home until her mother leaves.

496
00:37:41,545 --> 00:37:44,225
What good will all these outbursts do?

497
00:37:44,305 --> 00:37:45,585
I don't know.

498
00:37:53,385 --> 00:37:54,505
<i>Runch,</i>

499
00:37:54,585 --> 00:37:56,985
<i>I don't want to blame your mom, but,</i>

500
00:37:57,065 --> 00:38:00,465
<i>recording her conversation with Neen</i>
<i>so she could play it back to you?</i>

501
00:38:00,545 --> 00:38:02,265
<i>That doesn't seem natural at all.</i>

502
00:38:02,345 --> 00:38:03,665
What do you mean?

503
00:38:04,345 --> 00:38:05,865
<i>Have you ever seen a soap opera?</i>

504
00:38:05,945 --> 00:38:08,425
This is exactly like a soap opera plot.

505
00:38:08,505 --> 00:38:10,225
It's as if your mom had planned it,

506
00:38:10,305 --> 00:38:13,225
trying to make Neen
look like the bad guy to you.

507
00:38:13,865 --> 00:38:16,225
<i>Would my mom really go that far?</i>

508
00:38:18,185 --> 00:38:20,985
Mothers will do anything,

509
00:38:21,065 --> 00:38:24,145
especially one
who's as protective as yours.

510
00:38:24,225 --> 00:38:27,625
<i>She'd do it just so she wouldn't</i>
<i>lose you to someone else.</i>

511
00:38:28,145 --> 00:38:31,305
<i>I think you fell for your mother's trick.</i>

512
00:38:31,385 --> 00:38:35,105
<i>You'd better apologize to Neen</i>
<i>and win her back.</i>

513
00:38:44,105 --> 00:38:45,505
Hello, Dad.

514
00:38:46,025 --> 00:38:46,985
Hello, Mom.

515
00:38:47,065 --> 00:38:47,905
Hello.

516
00:38:49,345 --> 00:38:50,905
Hello, Nai.

517
00:38:53,945 --> 00:38:55,705
You see, I came here to--

518
00:38:55,785 --> 00:38:59,545
Runch, you don't have to say anything.
I know what happened.

519
00:39:05,665 --> 00:39:08,545
Does… Does everyone know already?

520
00:39:11,705 --> 00:39:14,985
It's not that hard to guess what happened.

521
00:39:22,145 --> 00:39:26,185
I'm sorry for yelling at Neen.

522
00:39:28,065 --> 00:39:32,305
Fighting is just part of a relationship.

523
00:39:37,825 --> 00:39:40,265
It doesn't matter whether you fight.

524
00:39:41,345 --> 00:39:43,905
What matters is whether
you still choose each other

525
00:39:44,985 --> 00:39:46,385
after you fight.

526
00:39:52,345 --> 00:39:53,985
I choose her.

527
00:39:55,265 --> 00:39:56,745
I always have.

528
00:39:57,705 --> 00:40:00,425
But sometimes,
I'm not so good at handling it.

529
00:40:03,745 --> 00:40:07,225
Neen's in her room.
You should go and see her.

530
00:40:12,065 --> 00:40:13,145
Okay.

531
00:40:18,065 --> 00:40:21,505
Neen. Can you open the door for me?

532
00:40:27,225 --> 00:40:28,505
Neen,

533
00:40:29,945 --> 00:40:32,425
I know you're listening.

534
00:40:35,385 --> 00:40:37,585
I've come to take you home.

535
00:40:43,585 --> 00:40:44,865
I'm not going.

536
00:40:46,105 --> 00:40:47,665
I'm sorry.

537
00:40:52,785 --> 00:40:56,065
I don't want to hear your apology.
Those are nothing but words.

538
00:40:56,625 --> 00:40:59,825
I want you to show me you're really sorry.

539
00:41:08,465 --> 00:41:10,665
What do you want me to do?

540
00:41:14,265 --> 00:41:16,545
Do whatever it takes
to make your mom leave,

541
00:41:16,625 --> 00:41:18,785
then I'll accept your apology.

542
00:41:38,625 --> 00:41:41,745
How'd it go, Runch?
Did she agree to come home?

543
00:41:43,665 --> 00:41:44,985
No.

544
00:41:45,065 --> 00:41:46,065
Oh dear.

545
00:41:46,145 --> 00:41:48,345
She's still mad at me, isn't she?

546
00:41:51,625 --> 00:41:55,465
It's my fault.
I'm the one who caused this.

547
00:41:55,545 --> 00:41:58,785
Had I not moved in and just stayed away,

548
00:41:59,305 --> 00:42:01,625
Neen wouldn't have been so mad at you.

549
00:42:02,265 --> 00:42:05,305
I'm getting too old.
I didn't think it through,

550
00:42:05,385 --> 00:42:07,345
and now I'm giving you a hard time.

551
00:42:11,505 --> 00:42:12,905
Mom.

552
00:42:15,505 --> 00:42:17,385
Please don't say that.

553
00:42:19,905 --> 00:42:21,585
Should I make up with her?

554
00:42:21,665 --> 00:42:24,425
I'll go and apologize.
I'll even bow down to her

555
00:42:24,505 --> 00:42:27,025
as long as she'll move back in with you.

556
00:42:27,785 --> 00:42:31,305
It's okay. I'll handle this myself.

557
00:42:31,385 --> 00:42:33,465
I'm worried, though.

558
00:42:33,545 --> 00:42:36,185
I'm scared she won't be back ever again.

559
00:42:39,545 --> 00:42:41,985
I won't give up so easily, Mom.

560
00:42:43,225 --> 00:42:46,585
I'll find a way to make up with her
and win her back.

561
00:42:48,185 --> 00:42:52,105
No matter how hard it is,
I won't let go of her hand.

562
00:42:53,185 --> 00:42:54,945
I believe in you, Runch.

563
00:43:47,105 --> 00:43:49,945
‎ONE YEAR AGO

564
00:43:58,345 --> 00:44:00,505
Finally, the day has come.

565
00:44:01,985 --> 00:44:04,505
The day we become each other's wives.

566
00:44:13,225 --> 00:44:15,745
And from this day forward,

567
00:44:17,065 --> 00:44:20,585
we'll be each other's wives forever.

568
00:44:24,465 --> 00:44:25,625
Yes, we will.

569
00:44:59,785 --> 00:45:02,025
You threw away my ring, didn't you?

570
00:45:02,105 --> 00:45:03,825
So that ring matters more than me?

571
00:45:03,905 --> 00:45:06,185
Couldn't keep up the act,
so you finally snapped?

572
00:45:06,265 --> 00:45:07,785
This was your plan, wasn't it?

573
00:45:07,865 --> 00:45:11,185
I'm an innocent girl.
I'd never scheme against you.

574
00:45:11,265 --> 00:45:12,145
You're so full of it!

575
00:45:12,225 --> 00:45:13,745
-Huh?
-Mom!

576
00:45:13,825 --> 00:45:16,065
-That's enough. Mom!
-You!

577
00:45:16,145 --> 00:45:18,425
Stop it! Don't you lay a finger on Neen.

578
00:45:18,505 --> 00:45:19,745
Don't hurt her.

579
00:45:19,825 --> 00:45:22,265
I know it must be difficult for you.

580
00:45:22,345 --> 00:45:24,705
If you want to talk or vent…

581
00:45:25,745 --> 00:45:27,705
<i>…I'm always here to listen.</i>

582
00:45:28,305 --> 00:45:32,065
Getting to hug you
is enough to cheer me up.

583
00:46:15,065 --> 00:46:17,065
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

